(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)) (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :forms :audit-ledger)) (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-framing-execution :authorize-structural-work :proceed-with-framing-work :commit-framing-decision :finalize-structural-framing-decision :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-site-safety-officer-judgment)) (:actor/robotics? true) (:adr/related (vector "2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage")) (:adr/status :accepted) (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the framing work" "finalize the framing work" "finalize the structural framing decision" "commit to the framing decision" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment")) (:adr/id 2799007119) (:actor/domain :trades/building-frame-crew-coordination) (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)) (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-site :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-op :unknown-crew :crew-wrong-site :scope-excluded-rationale)) (:registry/maturity :implemented) (:actor/isco-08 "7119") (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)) (:adr/doc_type "adr") (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)) (:operation/entry-point :intake) (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007119: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7119 Building Frame and Related Trades Workers Not Elsewhere Classified job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7119\n-- Building Frame and Related Trades Workers Not Elsewhere Classified**\nonly, Wave3 (production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7119\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7119\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Building Frame and Related Trades\nWorkers Not Elsewhere Classified\" -- confirming the premise, no\nmismatch, no truncation needing de-truncation. Prior to this ADR the\nentry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7119` (`gh api`\n404 confirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7119` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nBuilding Frame Trades Workers perform structural framing construction\nwork on active job sites -- real physical-safety stakes (falls,\nstructural collapse, equipment injury). The controlling constraint for\nthis vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op\nthat directly finalizes a structural-framing-execution decision, or\noverrides a site-safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to JOB-SITE\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs framing\nwork itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session. The named-scope-excluded-op\ndefense-in-depth layer was additionally adopted after reading the\nclosely-related concurrent sibling\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders, same wave, same job-site-scheduling/logistics-\ncoordination domain shape, landed in this same batch), whose ADR\n(2799007111) documents the identical two-layer op-exclusion pattern\n(generic closed-allowlist HARD check plus a second, independently-named\nconcretely-forbidden-op HARD check) this ADR also adopts.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7119` as an OSS job-site\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for building frame and related\ntrades crews, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Framing Crew\nAdvisor ⊣ FramingCrewGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **job-site scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct framing-work-execution authority** -- it must NEVER\nbe designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nstructural-framing-execution decision, or any override of a\nsite-safety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a structural-integrity/fall-hazard/\n  crew-fatigue concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- framing-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nstructural-framing-execution decision or a site-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-framing-execution` cannot even be proposed via a\nlegitimate request path that reaches an allowed disposition (the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check, `:unknown-op`, rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently the moment it appears as a proposal's\n`:op`, regardless of which code path produced it -- the default mock\nadvisor, a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, or a misbehaving\nfork). A second, independent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-op`)\nadditionally names seven concretely-forbidden ops\n(`framingcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-framing-execution`, `:authorize-structural-work`,\n`:proceed-with-framing-work`, `:commit-framing-decision`,\n`:finalize-structural-framing-decision`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-site-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, verified\nby dedicated unit and full-graph-integration tests\n(`framingcrew.governor-test/hard-on-named-scope-excluded-op-finalize-framing-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-named-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`framingcrew.actor-test/holds-a-named-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Six HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Site unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered job site (`:no-site`). Never trusts the\n   proposal's own claim of which site is in scope.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`) -- a claim to directly actuate outside\n   governance; the governor never dispatches hardware and never\n   finalizes a structural-framing-execution decision itself.\n3. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n4. **Named scope-excluded op** -- independently, any `:op` matching the\n   seven concretely-forbidden names above is a second HARD, PERMANENT\n   block (`:scope-excluded-op`), so an audit trail can distinguish\n   \"simply not on the allowlist\" from \"named specifically as a\n   forbidden finalization/override action.\"\n5. **Crew basis** -- a proposal citing a `:crew-id` must cite a\n   REGISTERED crew belonging to the request's own site\n   (`:unknown-crew` / `:crew-wrong-site`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/site\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any action.\n6. **Scope-excluded rationale** -- independent, defense-in-depth layer\n   on top of checks 3/4: even for an otherwise-allowed op, any proposal\n   whose free text (`:rationale` or `:description`) names a\n   finalization/execution ACTION for proceeding with or committing to\n   the framing work, or overriding the site safety officer's judgment\n   (`framingcrew.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`), is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-rationale`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content.\n\n### Two escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a structural-integrity/\n  fall-hazard/crew-fatigue observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds the\n  crew's registered `:max-supply-order-cost` (5000 in the test\n  fixtures, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-exact-ceiling-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-ceiling\n  framing-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  structural-framing-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"framing\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's\nown default rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the\nactor's own happy path -- this actor's own op is literally named\n`:flag-safety-concern`, so a bare \"safety\" term would self-trip on\nevery single legitimate safety-flag proposal (the mock advisor's\ndefault rationale template, `\"proposed \" (name op) \" for site \"\nsite-id`, literally renders to \"proposed flag-safety-concern for site\nsite-1\" for that op). `framingcrew.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (\"proceed with\nthe framing work\", \"override the site safety officer's judgment\",\netc.), never bare nouns, and\n`framingcrew.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the real default mock advisor (not a\nhand-built fixture), never trips either `:scope-excluded-rationale` or\n`:scope-excluded-op`. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment or verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7119\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7119` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7119`) and `:required-technologies` widened to\n  `[:robotics :identity :forms :audit-ledger]` to match `blueprint.edn`\n  (adding `:forms`, since this actor's ops are fundamentally job-site\n  data-entry/logging forms), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented count\n  bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately before\n  the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 20 tests, 54 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy), with a mojibake check (0 U+FFFD replacement\n  characters) on the Japanese-language violation-detail strings in\n  `framingcrew.governor`.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-framing-execution` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  structural-framing-execution decision exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe (falls,\n  structural collapse, equipment injury), the capability itself must\n  not exist. The only op related to site-safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/\n  site-safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes,\n  or defers a framing-execution decision for later automatic\n  execution.\n- Making the supply-order cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  3313 reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected\n  per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-ceiling framing-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the structural-framing-\n  execution/safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional\n  block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"framing\" \"safety\"]`):\n  rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug class described\n  above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this exact task) --\n  this actor's own op is literally named `:flag-safety-concern`, so a\n  bare \"safety\" term would self-trip on every legitimate safety-flag\n  proposal, and this domain necessarily discusses \"framing\" to do its\n  scheduling/logging job.\n- A single generic `:unknown-op` check with no separately-named\n  `scope-excluded-ops` set: considered sufficient on its own (the\n  closed allowlist already structurally excludes anything not in the\n  four legitimate ops), but the concurrently-landing sibling\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7111` (House Builders, same wave, same domain\n  shape) established a two-layer pattern in this same batch that gives\n  clearer audit-trail semantics (distinguishing \"not on the allowlist\"\n  from \"named specifically as a dangerous finalization/override\n  action\"); adopted for parity and stronger auditability rather than\n  left as a single generic check.\n- Merging `site` and `crew` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered site AND independently-registered crew\n  belonging to that site) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a\n  worker/site record must be independently verified/registered before\n  any action, and the established pattern from prior\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered site (and, when\n   crew-scoped, an independently registered crew belonging to that\n   site). Not a structural-framing-execution or safety-officer\n   decision in any respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a structural-framing-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-rationale` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific framing step -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a structural-integrity/\n   fall-hazard/crew-fatigue concern to a human/site safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the site safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- framing-materials procurement\n   proposal only (material, quantity, cost). Not a structural-framing-\n   execution or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above the crew's registered ceiling always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na structural-framing-execution decision or a site-safety-officer-\njudgment override -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`framingcrew.governor/known-ops`), (b) seven concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at both the governor-unit level and the\nfull-actor-graph level (`framingcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`framingcrew.governor-test/hard-on-named-scope-excluded-op-finalize-framing-execution`,\n`.../hard-on-named-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`framingcrew.actor-test/holds-a-named-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`framingcrew.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases`,\n`.../scope-violation-phrase`), tested directly against rationale/\ndescription text that attempts to proceed with the framing work or\noverride the site safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-\nallowlisted op\n(`framingcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-proceed-with-framing-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-safety-officer`).") (:adr/date "2026-07-17") (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 5000}") (:test/counts "{:total 20, :assertions 54, :failures 0, :errors 0}") (:actor/coordination? true) (:actor/name "Framing Crew Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice") (:db/id -1) (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :site-verification :crew-verification :closed-op-allowlist :named-scope-excluded-op-defense-in-depth :supply-order-cost-threshold-escalation)) (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7119") (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7119") (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7119)) (:test/simulator :framingcrew.actor-test) (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7119 — Building Frame and Related Trades Workers Not Elsewhere Classified Job-Site Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Coverage") (:adr/source-format "edn") (:adr/references (vector 2607121000 2799007111)) (:actor/wave 3) (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7119)))
